#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec05_wms-client/section.rst:57
msgid "``OFFSITE 0 0 0`` , ignore black background color"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec05_wms-client/section.rst:58
msgid "``STATUS OFF``, this layer is turned off by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec05_wms-client/section.rst:59
msgid "``CONNECTIONTYPE WMS`` Input layer connection use. Defaults to local ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec05_wms-client/section.rst:61
msgid ""
"If we had to be explicit, we would add all other vector and raster layers"
" locally in our MapFile CONNECTIONTYPE. Instead, we only define "
"connection types that are external. WMS is an external data layer from "
"other map servers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec05_wms-client/section.rst:66
msgid ""
"``CONNECTION \"http://webgis.pub/cgi-bin/mapserv?map=/owg/mfb2.map\"``, "
"the connection string that allows us to “get” data from another server. "
"In the case of a WMS connection, this is a URL. If we were using a "
"PostGIS database, this would be an SQL statement. Note that the string in"
" your MapFile is on a single line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec05_wms-client/section.rst:72
msgid ""
"``METADATA``, marks the metadata object of our WMS layer. MapServer uses "
"the parameters defined by this object, along with the above connection "
"parameters, to form valid WMS requests to the WMS server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec05_wms-client/section.rst:76
msgid ""
"``\"wms_srs\" \"epsg:4326\"`` , WMS projection. Sometimes WMS servers "
"support multiple projections. If that’s the case, you’ll probably want to"
" ask for your output projection (``EPSG:2163``) map. Unfortunately, "
"external WMS servers do not support this kind of projection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec05_wms-client/section.rst:81
msgid ""
"``\"wms_name\" \"modis\"`` , the name of the WMS layer to add. It’s like "
"adding the parameter ``\"layers=modis\"`` ,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec05_wms-client/section.rst:84
msgid ""
"``\"wms_server_version\" \"1.1.1\"`` , the version of the server for the "
"WMS version. More supported versions can be viewed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec05_wms-client/section.rst:87
msgid ""
"``\"wms_format\" \"image/jpeg\"`` , the image format we expect to receive"
" from the WMS server. You can try ``image/png`` or other allowed values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec05_wms-client/section.rst:91
msgid "Additional information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec05_wms-client/section.rst:93
msgid ""
"To learn more about adding WMS layers to your application, visit the WMS "
"client how to record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec05_wms-client/section.rst:96
msgid ""
"In addition to adding WMS layer objects, there is also the next new "
"object for the map. This is the Web object. There are two parameters in "
"the Web object:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec05_wms-client/section.rst:100
msgid ""
"``IMAGEPATH '/data/tmp/'`` , the local absolute path to the temporary "
"directory for web access. The user running the web server process should "
"be able to write to this directory. Make sure the path contains the last "
"slash ( ``/`` ). (Your IMAGEPATH might look like this: \\`\\ "
"``/home/apache/htdocs/tmp/`` or ``C:/Inetpub/wwwroot/tmp/``.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec05_wms-client/section.rst:106
msgid ""
"``IMAGEURL '/tmp/'`` , which is how IMAGEPATH appears relative to the web"
" server’s root directory. If we had to enter the full URL, it would be "
"“http://terrasip.gis.umn.edu/tmp/” . Make sure the path contains the last"
" slash ( ``/`` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec05_wms-client/section.rst:111
msgid ""
"Finally, a new parameter has been added to the ``MAP`` object: ``NAME`` ."
" This is the identifier of the map object. MapServer creates and dumps a "
"``tmp`` directory for all images using this prefix. It’s not really "
"needed in this example, but it won’t have any bad effects either."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec05_wms-client/section.rst:116
msgid ""
"If you want to share your data layer to other map servers, you need to "
"add ``METADATA`` object to your ``MAP`` object, and add ``METADATA`` "
"object to each layer object you want to share with everyone. All WMS "
"layers added from another server are automatically cascaded and made "
"available to others (contagious). For details on how to make your "
"MapServer application a WMS server, please read the WMS server "
"documentation carefully. In addition, in addition to the WMS service, "
"MapServer also supports the WFS service, you can check the documentation "
"to learn how to configure MapServer to implement a WFS server, or a WFS "
"client."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec06_group/section.rst:4
msgid "Draw maps with style layer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec06_group/section.rst:6
msgid ""
"More advanced WMSs use “style layers” to describe a map. A style layer "
"can be thought of as a transparent layer composed of symbolic elements. A"
" map is composed of these style layers in a certain order, which is "
"usually called Z-value order. Users can define complex or simple maps by "
"adding or removing style layers. A style layer is actually a combination "
"of a layer and a style. Conceptually, the layer defines a stream of "
"features, and the style defines how those features are symbolized. In a "
"WMS process, the drawing style of a map is specified according to the "
"LAYERS and STYLES request parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec06_group/section.rst:17
msgid "Support for named styles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec06_group/section.rst:19
msgid ""
"Named styles support are introduced in MapServer 5.2. The support is base"
" on MS RFC 39: Support of WMS/SLD Named Styles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec06_group/section.rst:22
msgid ""
"MapServer 5.2 introduces the possibility to assign a group to a series of"
" classes defined on a layer object using two new non-mandatory keywords "
"CLASSGROUP (at the layer level) and GROUP at the class level:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb5_mapserver-wms/sec06_group/section.rst:49
msgid ""
"At rendering time, if the CLASSGROUP is defined, only classes that have "
"the same group name would be used. Based on this concept, WMS/SLD support"
" uses the class groups as named styles. Each group of classes is "
"considered equivalent to a named style:"
msgstr ""

